{
  "intro": [
    "Xenon is four pieces that talk to each other:",
    "",
    "- **The engine** (`server/`, Node.js): a small local web server on `127.0.0.1:3030`. It reads the PC, runs actions and keeps the data.",
    "- **The screen** (`server/index.html`, `server/js/`, `server/components/`, `server/styles/`): the dashboard, a web page the engine serves. A phone opens the same page.",
    "- **The app** (`apps/native/`, Rust + Tauri): the window that shows the screen, starts the engine and draws widgets over the desktop.",
    "- **The helpers** (`helper/` in C#, `helper-mac/` in Swift): small programs for the things only the operating system can do.",
    "",
    "Below, every feature has one line saying what it does and where its files are. A file belongs to the first feature that names it."
  ],
  "areas": [
    {
      "id": "engine",
      "name": "Engine",
      "what": "The program behind everything: it starts, answers the screen, saves settings, updates itself."
    },
    {
      "id": "dashboard",
      "name": "Dashboard",
      "what": "The screen itself: the grid of tiles, how it looks, the top bar, the scenes shown when idle."
    },
    {
      "id": "widgets",
      "name": "Widgets",
      "what": "One row per tile on the dashboard."
    },
    {
      "id": "bit",
      "name": "Bit and AI",
      "what": "The assistant: chat, voice, memory and the things it can do on the PC."
    },
    {
      "id": "store",
      "name": "Store and supporters",
      "what": "The catalog of looks and widgets, and what supporters get."
    },
    {
      "id": "desktop",
      "name": "On top of the desktop",
      "what": "What Xenon shows outside the dashboard: widgets on the desktop, the menu, alerts, captures."
    },
    {
      "id": "apps",
      "name": "Connected apps",
      "what": "Other programs Xenon talks to."
    },
    {
      "id": "makers",
      "name": "For widget makers",
      "what": "What lets other people build widgets safely."
    },
    {
      "id": "native",
      "name": "App and helpers",
      "what": "The native programs around the engine, and the code that differs per operating system."
    },
    {
      "id": "upkeep",
      "name": "Repo upkeep",
      "what": "Tests, tools, the website and the project files."
    }
  ],
